    const root=document.createElement('div');root.className='curioid-os-studio';root.innerHTML=`<section class="cos-panel is-simple-mode" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="CURIOID Sandbox OS"><header class="cos-header"><div><small>CURIOID / PERSONAL OS BUILDER</small><h2>Sandbox OS</h2><p>One local workshop. Build Basic, Advanced or Hybrid.</p></div><button type="button" data-cos-close aria-label="Close Sandbox OS">×</button></header><nav class="cos-tabs"><button type="button" data-cos-tab="build" aria-selected="true">Build an OS</button><button type="button" data-cos-tab="worlds" aria-selected="false">My OS</button><button type="button" data-cos-tab="sdk" aria-selected="false">Developer SDK</button><button type="button" data-cos-tab="submit" aria-selected="false">Review &amp; export</button></nav><div class="cos-tab-panel" data-cos-panel="build"><fieldset class="cos-mode-switch cos-mode-choices" aria-label="Choose how to build your Sandbox OS"><legend>Choose your build style</legend><label class="cos-mode-choice"><input type="radio" name="cos-builder-mode" data-cos-mode-choice value="simple" checked><span><b>Basic</b><small>Pick ready-made tools and design your OS without code.</small></span></label><label class="cos-mode-choice"><input type="radio" name="cos-builder-mode" data-cos-mode-choice value="advanced"><span><b>Advanced</b><small>Build the interface and logic yourself with the isolated Worker SDK.</small></span></label><label class="cos-mode-choice"><input type="radio" name="cos-builder-mode" data-cos-mode-choice value="hybrid"><span><b>Hybrid</b><small>Start with Basic modules, then add your own HTML, CSS, Worker logic and Connect features.</small></span></label></fieldset><p class="cos-mode-description" data-cos-mode-description>Basic is the easiest way to begin. Start blank or choose a recipe, then add only the pieces you need.</p><p class="cos-mode-draft-note">Basic, Advanced and Hybrid drafts auto-save locally in this browser, including your code and attached assets. Close the workshop or browser safely and your last draft will be recovered when you return. Nothing is uploaded.</p><p class="cos-note" data-cos-draft-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Local autosave is ready.</p><div class="cos-builder-grid"><div class="cos-fields"><label>OS name<input data-cos-name maxlength="80" value="My Curious OS"></label><label class="cos-advanced-fields" hidden>OS ID<input data-cos-id maxlength="40" value="my-curious-os"><small>Advanced setting. In Basic mode this is generated from your OS name.</small></label><label class="cos-advanced-fields" hidden>Version<input data-cos-version value="1.0.0" maxlength="32"></label><label class="cos-advanced-fields" hidden>Required Kernel version<input data-cos-requires-kernel value="1.3.0" maxlength="32"><small>Minimum CURIOID Kernel version. Your package will be rejected on older versions.</small></label><label class="cos-advanced-fields" hidden>Required Connect version range<input data-cos-requires-connect value="^1.0.0" maxlength="100"><small>Semantic version range, for example ^1.0.0 or &gt;=1.0.0 &lt;2.0.0.</small></label><label class="cos-advanced-fields" hidden>Creator / author<input data-cos-author maxlength="100" placeholder="Your creator name"><small>Optional. Defaults to Independent creator when left blank.</small></label><label class="cos-wide">Description<textarea data-cos-description rows="2" maxlength="500" placeholder="What makes this world different?">A personal workspace made around the things that matter to you.</textarea></label><section class="cos-simple-builder cos-wide"><header><div><small>01 / MAKE IT YOURS</small><b>Choose a starting world</b><p>These are starting points, not restrictions. Change any tool, color or layout to make it yours.</p></div><span>NO CODE REQUIRED</span></header><label data-cos-step-target="start">What is this OS for?<select data-cos-template><option value="blank">Blank OS · choose every piece yourself</option><option value="personal">Personal Desk · everyday workspace</option><option value="study">Study Hub · learning and focus</option><option value="creator">Creator Studio · ideas and projects</option><option value="home">Home Organizer · household and planning</option><option value="journal">Minimal Journal · writing and collections</option><option value="developer">Developer Desk · projects and bug tracking</option><option value="library">Media Library · books, games and watchlist</option><option value="storyteller">Storyteller Studio · characters and prompts</option><option value="kitchen">Kitchen Desk · recipes and inventory</option><option value="explorer">Explorer Desk · places and travel notes</option><option value="active">Activity Desk · habits and workouts</option><option value="sports">Sports Club · teams, events and training</option><option value="science">Science Lab · research and experiments</option><option value="gaming">Gaming Lounge · games, events and collections</option><option value="music">Music Room · creative projects and collections</option><option value="reading">Reading Nook · books, notes and focus</option><option value="cinema">Cinema Club · films, watchlists and events</option><option value="travel">Travel Planner · destinations and itineraries</option><option value="wellness">Wellness Space · habits and activity</option><option value="finance">Personal Admin · household records and planning</option><option value="garden">Garden Desk · plants, plans and inventory</option><option value="social">Community Hub · meetups and shared interests</option><option value="petcare">Pet Care Desk · routines and records</option><option value="learning">Learning Studio · study plans and reading</option><option value="workstation">Workstation OS · all-purpose productivity hub</option><option value="sportsdesk">Sports Performance OS · training, teams and events</option><option value="esports">Esports Command OS · gaming, tournaments and stats</option><option value="streamer">Creator &amp; Streaming OS · content production station</option><option value="researcher">Research OS · sources, notes and projects</option><option value="writer">Writer OS · drafting, characters and ideas</option><option value="financepro">Personal Finance OS · household administration</option><option value="eventhub">Event Operations OS · schedules and logistics</option><option value="fitnesslab">Fitness Lab OS · habits and training</option><option value="gamedev">Game Development OS · bugs, assets and builds</option><option value="soundlab">Audio Production OS · sound projects and assets</option><option value="movieclub">Cinema &amp; TV OS · watchlists and screenings</option><option value="bookclub">Reading Club OS · books and discussions</option><option value="homelab">Homelab OS · systems and maintenance</option><option value="gardenlab">Garden &amp; Grow OS · plants and seasonal work</option></select></label><label>Welcome message<input data-cos-tagline maxlength="120" value="Your own space, arranged your way."></label><div class="cos-simple-grid" data-cos-step-target="style"><label>Symbol<input data-cos-symbol maxlength="2" value="✳" aria-label="Your OS symbol"></label><label>Color world<select data-cos-theme><option value="midnight">Midnight mint</option><option value="ocean">Ocean blue</option><option value="forest">Forest green</option><option value="plum">Dreamy plum</option><option value="paper">Warm paper</option><option value="ember">Ember orange</option><option value="graphite">Graphite</option><option value="crimson">Crimson</option><option value="lavender">Lavender</option><option value="rose">Rose</option><option value="cobalt">Cobalt</option><option value="arctic">Arctic</option><option value="sunrise">Sunrise</option><option value="neon">Neon moss</option><option value="slate">Slate</option><option value="mint">Fresh mint</option></select></label><label>Visual style<select data-cos-look><option value="clean">Clean and focused</option><option value="soft">Soft and rounded</option><option value="terminal">Retro terminal</option><option value="playful">Playful and expressive</option></select></label><label>Navigation<select data-cos-layout><option value="side">Side menu</option><option value="top">Top menu</option></select></label></div><div class="cos-builder-steps" aria-label="Guided OS building steps"><button type="button" class="cos-builder-step" data-cos-step-jump="start"><span>01</span><b>Choose a starting point</b><small>Begin blank or use a recipe. You can change everything.</small><em>Go to start ↓</em></button><button type="button" class="cos-builder-step" data-cos-step-jump="modules"><span>02</span><b>Pick your modules</b><small>Mix Basic tools, App Library modules and ready-made collections.</small><em>Choose pieces ↓</em></button><button type="button" class="cos-builder-step" data-cos-step-jump="custom"><span>03</span><b>Create something new</b><small>Build your own private data tool without writing code.</small><em>Make a module ↓</em></button><button type="button" class="cos-builder-step" data-cos-step-jump="style"><span>04</span><b>Make it yours</b><small>Choose a theme, layout and visual style, then launch.</small><em>Style it ↓</em></button></div><p class="cos-note cos-builder-hint">Choose a recipe above to prefill your workspace, or leave it blank and add exactly the pieces you want below.</p><div class="cos-tool-heading"><b>Build your own OS from ready-made pieces</b><small>Add one at a time using the dropdown, or use a preset above. Reorder or remove anything later.</small></div><div class="cos-module-picker-row" data-cos-step-target="modules"><label>Choose a module<select data-cos-module-picker><option value="">Select a module to add…</option><optgroup label="Basic OS essentials"><option value="notes">✎ Notes</option><option value="tasks">✓ Tasks</option><option value="planner">▦ Planner</option><option value="bookmarks">◇ Bookmarks</option><option value="collections">▤ Collections</option><option value="calculator">＋ Calculator</option><option value="focus">◷ Focus timer</option></optgroup><optgroup label="App Library & OS modules"><option value="reading-log">📚 Reading Log</option><option value="idea-vault">💡 Idea Vault</option><option value="asset-catalog">🗂️ Asset Catalog</option><option value="habit-tracker">🌱 Habit Tracker</option><option value="content-calendar">🗓️ Content Calendar</option><option value="project-tracker">🧭 Project Tracker</option><option value="bug-tracker">🐛 Bug Tracker</option></optgroup><optgroup label="More ready-made collections"><option value="recipe-box">🍲 Recipe Box</option><option value="media-watchlist">🎬 Media Watchlist</option><option value="game-backlog">🎮 Game Backlog</option><option value="places-list">🧭 Places to Explore</option><option value="character-bible">🧙 Character Bible</option><option value="workout-log">🏃 Activity Log</option><option value="prompt-library">✨ Prompt Library</option><option value="inventory">📦 Personal Inventory</option><option value="event-planner">🎟️ Event Planner</option></optgroup><optgroup label="Your custom modules" data-cos-custom-options></optgroup></select></label><button type="button" data-cos-module-add class="cos-module-add">＋ Add module</button></div><div class="cos-module-selection"><div class="cos-module-selection-head"><b>Your OS modules</b><span data-cos-module-count>0 selected · 20 maximum</span></div><div class="cos-module-selection-list" data-cos-module-list><p class="cos-empty">Your OS is blank. Add a module from the library above, or make your own below.</p></div></div><p class="cos-note cos-module-origin-note">These modules reuse validated data fields from CURIOID tools. Your OS gets its own private records; original app scripts, network permissions and device access are never copied.</p><details class="cos-custom-module-builder" data-cos-step-target="custom"><summary>＋ Create my own module without code</summary><div class="cos-custom-module-intro"><b>Make a tool for anything you want to keep track of.</b><p>For example: recipes, games to try, characters, equipment, places to visit, workout sessions or video ideas.</p></div><div class="cos-custom-module-fields"><label>Module name<input data-cos-custom-name maxlength="50" placeholder="My recipe box"></label><label>Icon<input data-cos-custom-icon maxlength="4" value="▦" placeholder="✳"></label><label class="module-description-field">What is it for?<input data-cos-custom-description maxlength="180" placeholder="A private collection for my recipes"></label></div><div class="cos-custom-field-editor"><div class="cos-custom-field-row"><label>Field label<input data-cos-custom-field-label maxlength="60" placeholder="Recipe name"></label><label>Type<select data-cos-custom-field-type><option value="text">Short text</option><option value="textarea">Long text</option><option value="number">Number</option><option value="date">Date</option><option value="datetime-local">Date and time</option><option value="url">Web link</option><option value="email">Email address</option><option value="tel">Phone number</option><option value="color">Color</option><option value="select">Dropdown</option><option value="checkbox">Yes / no</option></select></label><label class="cos-custom-field-options" hidden>Dropdown choices<input data-cos-custom-field-options maxlength="240" placeholder="To try, Cooking, Favourite"></label><label class="cos-custom-field-required"><input type="checkbox" data-cos-custom-field-required> Required</label><button type="button" data-cos-custom-field-add>Add field</button></div><div class="cos-custom-field-list" data-cos-custom-field-list><p class="cos-empty">Add at least one field to define your new module.</p></div></div><div class="cos-custom-module-actions"><button type="button" data-cos-custom-module-create class="cos-primary">Create and add module</button><small>Up to 8 custom modules, 8 fields each. Everything is saved inside your local OS package.</small></div></details><p class="cos-note">Every Basic OS automatically includes private saving, backup/restore and a shareable workspace snapshot for CURIOID Exchange. No coding or configuration is needed.</p></section><section class="cos-advanced-fields cos-wide" hidden><div class="cos-advanced-section-head"><small>02 / ADVANCED BUILDER</small><b>Everything unlocked</b><p>Custom capabilities, artifact types, source code and bundled assets. Worlds communicate through CURIOID services and permissions. These controls are hidden in Simple mode so beginners can focus on building.</p></div><label>Capabilities this OS provides<textarea data-cos-capabilities rows="3" placeholder="greeting|Greeting service|Returns a greeting to other experiences">greeting|Greeting service|Returns a greeting to other experiences|granted</textarea><small>One per line: id|Name|Description|access. The optional final field is public or granted (default granted). Implement each through CurioidOS.onCapability().</small></label><label>Capability contracts JSON<textarea data-cos-contracts rows="6" spellcheck="false">{}</textarea><small>Optional JSON Schema by capability ID. Define input and output objects, for example {"greeting":{"input":{"type":"object","required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":80}},"additionalProperties":false},"output":{"type":"object"}}}.</small></label><label>Artifact types this OS can exchange<input data-cos-types value="my-world/note" placeholder="my-world/note, my-world/collection"><small>Comma-separated namespaced artifact types. Implement export and import handlers through the SDK.</small></label><label>Artifact contracts JSON<textarea data-cos-artifact-contracts rows="5" spellcheck="false">{}</textarea><small>Optional JSON Schema by artifact type. Only listed artifact types can have contracts.</small></label><label>Events this OS provides<textarea data-cos-events rows="5" spellcheck="false">[]</textarea><small>JSON array of event declarations, for example [{"id":"collection.updated","version":"1.0.0","access":"granted","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"collectionId":{"type":"string"}}}}]. Register the same event through CurioidOS.connect.registerEvent() before publishing it.</small></label><label>Messages this OS accepts<textarea data-cos-messages rows="6" spellcheck="false">[]</textarea><small>JSON array of request types with id, version, access, schema and optional outputContract. Register each handler with CurioidOS.connect.onMessage().</small></label><label>What this OS needs from other worlds<textarea data-cos-consumes rows="7" spellcheck="false">{
  "capabilities": [],
  "artifactTypes": [],
  "events": [],
  "messages": []
}</textarea><small>JSON lists of required capability IDs, artifact types, event IDs and message types. For events and messages, use objects with an id and optional ownerExperienceId to identify the provider.</small></label><p class="cos-note cos-network-note">Custom OS previews and coding tools block fetch-style requests, sockets, forms and remote resources; there is no optional internet permission. The embedded OS cannot navigate the CURIOID host page, but browsers do not reliably block navigation of the embedded frame itself, which may contact an external server. Run only code you trust. Your OS can still cooperate with other worlds through explicitly granted CURIOID capabilities, artifacts, services and Exchange.</p><div class="cos-actions"><button type="button" data-cos-regenerate>Regenerate source from my Basic setup</button></div></section></div><div class="cos-source-fields cos-advanced-fields" hidden><div class="cos-advanced-section-head"><small>03 / SOURCE EDITOR</small><b>Your OS, down to the code</b><p>Advanced mode gives you the full source. Hybrid mode keeps the generated Basic OS and treats these fields as optional additions. New logic runs in the isolated Worker.</p></div><p class="cos-hybrid-source-note" data-cos-hybrid-note hidden>HYBRID ADD-ONS · The Basic OS interface stays in place. Add a small HTML fragment, extra CSS or Worker logic here. The legacy UI-thread JavaScript field is disabled in Hybrid mode.</p><label data-cos-source-html>HTML<textarea data-cos-html spellcheck="false" rows="10"></textarea></label><label data-cos-source-css>CSS<textarea data-cos-css spellcheck="false" rows="10"></textarea></label><button type="button" data-cos-show-legacy hidden>Show legacy JavaScript compatibility editor</button><label data-cos-source-js hidden>Legacy JavaScript (compatibility only, runs on the OS UI thread)<textarea data-cos-js spellcheck="false" rows="10"></textarea><small>Compatibility mode only. This code runs on its sandboxed iframe thread, not the main CURIOID page. The parent watchdog warns after a prolonged missed heartbeat but does not close the entire world automatically. The desktop remains available so you can restart or close it yourself. Use the Worker editor for new logic. Browsers do not provide a hard memory quota.</small></label><label data-cos-source-worker>Isolated Worker JavaScript (recommended)<textarea data-cos-worker-js spellcheck="false" rows="12" placeholder="CurioidOS.ui.on('click', event => { /* respond to a data-os-id control */ });"></textarea><small>Runs in a dedicated Worker, away from the OS UI thread. Its watchdog terminates it after 15 seconds without a heartbeat while the tab is visible, and pauses checks while the tab is hidden. Limits: 180 host requests per minute, 16 concurrent requests, 24 MB of request data and 48 MB of response data per minute, 30 UI updates per second (128 KB of text per second), a 260,000-character Worker source cap, 128 active timers, 32 app intervals plus one reserved heartbeat, and 20,000 timer callbacks per minute. Host calls time out after 15 seconds; an unresponsive Worker is stopped after 15 seconds while the tab is visible. Use CurioidOS.info.workerLimits to inspect the enforced limits. Use CurioidOS.storage, CurioidOS.host, CurioidOS.ui and CurioidOS.request. The worker has no direct DOM or external network access. Browsers do not expose a portable hard Worker memory quota. Give each target element an id and the same data-os-id value, then update it with CurioidOS.ui.setText, setValue, setHidden or setDisabled. Example HTML: &lt;button id="run-button" data-os-id="run-button"&gt;Run&lt;/button&gt; and &lt;output id="status" data-os-id="status"&gt;Ready&lt;/output&gt;. Example Worker: CurioidOS.ui.on('click', event =&gt; { if (event.id === 'run-button') CurioidOS.ui.setText('status', 'Worker finished'); });</small></label></div></div><section class="cos-assets-box cos-advanced-fields" hidden><div><b>Local asset library</b><small>Attach images, audio, video, fonts or data files. Maximum 24 files, 2 MB each and 4 MB combined. Access them with CurioidOS.assets.list() / get(name).</small></div><label class="cos-import-button">Add assets<input type="file" data-cos-assets multiple accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp,image/gif,audio/mpeg,audio/wav,audio/ogg,audio/mp4,video/mp4,video/webm,font/woff,font/woff2,application/json,text/plain,text/csv"></label><div class="cos-asset-list" data-cos-asset-list>No local assets attached.</div></section><div class="cos-actions"><button type="button" data-cos-save class="cos-primary">Save locally</button><button type="button" data-cos-launch>Save &amp; launch</button><button type="button" data-cos-export>Download .curioidos</button><button type="button" data-cos-new>Reset to starter</button><label class="cos-import-button">Import a .curioidos<input type="file" data-cos-import accept=".curioidos,.json,application/json"></label></div><p class="cos-note" data-cos-build-status>OS packages and their data stay in this browser. New logic runs in a dedicated Worker. Legacy iframe JavaScript is available only when you explicitly open the compatibility editor or edit an existing legacy world. Nothing is published automatically.</p></div><div class="cos-tab-panel" data-cos-panel="worlds" hidden><div class="cos-panel-heading"><div><b>Your OS library</b><p>Saved operating systems are private to this browser profile. Other visitors cannot see or run them.</p></div><button type="button" data-cos-refresh>Refresh list</button></div><div class="cos-world-metrics" data-cos-world-metrics>Checking local registry…</div><div class="cos-orphan-tools" data-cos-orphan-tools hidden></div><div class="cos-world-backup-tools"><button type="button" data-cos-registry-backup>Backup entire universe</button><label class="cos-import-button">Restore universe backup<input type="file" data-cos-registry-restore accept=".curioidregistry,.json,application/json"></label></div><div class="cos-world-list" data-cos-world-list>Loading local worlds…</div><label class="cos-import-button">Restore one OS + local data backup<input type="file" data-cos-backup-import accept=".curioidbackup,.json,application/json"></label><small>Individual backups replace only the selected OS after confirmation. Universe backups append missing worlds and never overwrite existing ones.</small></div><div class="cos-tab-panel" data-cos-panel="sdk" hidden><div class="cos-sdk-copy"><h3>CURIOID OS SDK / v2 with Connect</h3><p>Your world is an independent experience running in a sandboxed frame. The parent page exposes only the CURIOID SDK bridge. Your world has private storage, internal clipboard access, and no external network or device access.</p><h4>Local storage</h4><p>Basic Builder worlds run their app logic in a dedicated Worker. The simple set/remove methods remain available for convenience, but use the version-aware methods below whenever two tabs or independent tasks could edit the same record. Stale revisions are rejected instead of silently overwriting newer work.</p><pre>// Read a value and its compare-and-set revision.
const snapshot = await CurioidOS.storage.getVersioned('draft');

// Save only if no other tab has changed this key.
const saved = await CurioidOS.storage.setIfRevision(
  'draft', { title: 'Hello' }, snapshot.revision
);

// Later, delete only the exact version you reviewed.
await CurioidOS.storage.removeIfRevision('draft', saved.revision);
</pre><p class="cos-note">getVersioned returns { key, value, revision, exists, deleted }. New keys start at revision 0. A failed revision check throws a conflict error; reload the latest record before retrying. Existing set/get/remove methods remain backward-compatible.</p>
await CurioidOS.clipboard.writeText('A note inside CURIOID');
const copied = await CurioidOS.clipboard.readText();</pre><h4>Artifacts and capabilities</h4><pre>const artifacts = await CurioidOS.artifacts.list({ limit: 30 });\n// Creation requires a manifest-declared type and user confirmation.\nawait CurioidOS.artifacts.create({\n  type: 'my-world/note', title: 'A note', data: { text: 'Hello' }\n});\nconst availableTools = await CurioidOS.capabilities.list();\n// Public calls need your approval; granted calls also need an owner grant.\nawait CurioidOS.capabilities.call('echonoise.lexicon.analyze', { text: 'Neon rivers' });\n// Review grants for capabilities your OS provides.\nconst grants = await CurioidOS.permissions.list();\n// Grant or revoke access for another currently open experience.\nawait CurioidOS.permissions.grant('useros.my-world.greeting', 'useros:another-world');\nawait CurioidOS.permissions.revoke('useros.my-world.greeting', 'useros:another-world');
// Each OS has private, namespaced local data services.
const services = CurioidOS.services.catalogue();
await CurioidOS.services.put('personal-items', { id:'idea-1', kind:'note', title:'My idea', data:{ body:'A new thought' } });
const notes = await CurioidOS.services.list('personal-items');
const backup = await CurioidOS.services.exportBackup();</pre><p>Local service records belong to this OS. Other worlds cannot read them directly; share selected content as a Kernel artifact or capability. Backups can include local service records.</p><h4>Bundled assets and public Kernel events</h4><pre>const assets = CurioidOS.assets.list();
const logo = CurioidOS.assets.get('logo.png');
const stop = CurioidOS.events.on(event => {
  console.log(event.type, event.artifactId);
});
// Call stop() to unsubscribe.</pre><h4>Join the Kernel as a capability provider</h4><pre>CurioidOS.onCapability(async ({ id, input }) => {\n  if (id === 'greeting') return { message: 'Hello from my OS', input };\n  throw new Error('Unknown capability');\n});</pre><h4>CURIOID Connect: discover and message another world</h4><pre>const connectInfo = await CurioidOS.connect.info();
const myManifest = await CurioidOS.connect.manifest();
const tools = await CurioidOS.connect.discover({ query: 'phonetic' });

// Register a typed event before publishing it.
await CurioidOS.connect.registerEvent({
  id: 'note-created', version: '1.0.0', access: 'granted',
  schema: { type: 'object', required: ['title'],
    properties: { title: { type: 'string', maxLength: 120 } },
    additionalProperties: false }
});
await CurioidOS.connect.publishEvent('note-created', { title: 'A new thought' });
await CurioidOS.connect.grantEvent('note-created', 'aether-os');
const stopEvents = await CurioidOS.connect.onEvent('aether-os', 'collection-updated', event => { console.log(event.detail); });

// Receive a typed internal message. Access defaults to grant-controlled.
const stopMessages = await CurioidOS.connect.onMessage('request-summary',
  async ({ payload, fromExperienceId }) => ({ summary: String(payload.text).slice(0, 240) }),
  { access: 'granted', schema: { type: 'object', required: ['text'],
      properties: { text: { type: 'string', maxLength: 4000 } },
      additionalProperties: false },
    outputContract: { type: 'object', required: ['summary'],
      properties: { summary: { type: 'string', maxLength: 240 } },
      additionalProperties: false } }
);
// Grant only after opening the requesting world.
await CurioidOS.connect.grantMessage('request-summary', 'aether-os');
// Another world can send to this OS using its scoped Connect client.
// await anotherWorld.sendMessage('useros.my-world', 'request-summary', { text: 'Hello' });
</pre><h4>Native Exchange adapter</h4><pre>CurioidOS.onExport(async () => [{\n  type: 'my-world/note', title: 'My note', data: { text: 'Hello' }\n}]);\nCurioidOS.onImport(async ({ payload, meta }) => {\n  await CurioidOS.storage.set('received', payload);\n  return { imported: true };\n});</pre><p><b>Security model:</b> sandbox omits allow-same-origin, forms, popups and top-level navigation. HTML event handlers, external scripts, frames and forms are stripped. External network requests are blocked for all user-created worlds. Internal CURIOID capabilities are available through explicit permissions. Kernel calls and artifact creation are individually confirmed.</p></div></div><div class="cos-tab-panel" data-cos-panel="submit" hidden><div class="cos-submit-grid"><div><h3>Review or export your OS</h3><p>Your OS works privately in this browser. Save a review package, download it from Browser Vault, then attach it to an email for manual review.</p><p class="cos-note">Nothing is uploaded or sent automatically. You choose whether to open your email app and send the package yourself. Publisher contact: ninewinters@hotmail.com.</p><div class="cos-actions"><button type="button" class="cos-primary" data-cos-submit>Save review package</button><button type="button" data-cos-review-download>Save another copy to Vault</button><button type="button" data-cos-copy-submission>Copy package summary</button></div><p data-cos-submit-status aria-live="polite">A package contains your OS settings, source and local assets. It stays on this device unless you choose to share it.</p></div><div><h3>Open a review package locally</h3><p>Inspect a package from another person and add it to this browser’s My OS list. It will not be published to the website.</p><label class="cos-import-button">Choose a review package<input type="file" data-cos-review-import accept=".curioid-review,.curioidos,.json,application/json"></label><div data-cos-review-result class="cos-review-result">No review package loaded.</div><button type="button" data-cos-review-approve disabled>Add to My OS</button><p class="cos-note">Nothing is installed until you approve it. This is a local import tool, not a public publishing service.</p></div></div></div></section>`;
