        const specimens=[['Glasswing Nocturne','Clear wings with a narrow silver margin. Recorded near interior windows after rain.','Wings remain transparent even when the specimen is not facing a light.'],['Ivory Stair Moth','Pale cream wings with a faint stair-step edge. Usually found near landings.','Its resting position is always one step above the last observation.'],['Blue Receipt Moth','A folded-paper pattern across the hindwings.','The wing markings resemble totals from purchases nobody remembers making.'],['Velvet Hinge Moth','Dark plum thorax and soft bronze wing spots.','The species appears to prefer doors that have not been installed.'],['Clockface Moth','Circular markings resemble an analogue dial.','The markings change by one minute when viewed indirectly.'],['Ashen Lantern Moth','Warm grey wings and pale antennae.','It gathers near lamps that are switched off.'],['Northbound Moth','Thin green bands that point toward the nearest wall.','Every recorded specimen was facing north, including in the southern room.'],['Paper Window Moth','Matte wings with a rectangular transparent patch.','The patch is darker than the surrounding wing when held up to light.'],['Morrow Moth','A small ochre species with a double tail.','It has been logged one day before it was first seen.'],['Quiet Bell Moth','Round wings marked with two pale circles.','No sound is produced when it moves. The room sometimes rings.'],['Basement Pearl Moth','Grey-white scales with a faint blue sheen.','The specimen is cold to the touch, even in a warm room.'],['Room Zero Moth','Unusually symmetrical and difficult to photograph.','Photographs show a second pair of wings that are absent from the specimen.'],['Moth of the Third Key','Three dark dots form a keyhole shape.','The keyhole is not present in the same place twice.'],['Window Dust Moth','Fine beige scales with a translucent fringe.','It leaves a clean rectangle on dusty glass.'],['Late Summer Moth','Rust-red edge with a yellow centre.','Its season begins after the building records the end of summer.'],['Corridor Moth','Long narrow wings, almost folded shut.','It has been observed crossing the same corridor in both directions at once.'],['Unsent Letter Moth','Blue-grey wings with a crease down the centre.','The species is attracted to envelopes that have already been opened.'],['Reverse Lantern Moth','Dark wings with a pale body.','The light appears to be behind the body rather than in front.'],['Thin Snow Moth','White wings, nearly invisible against paper.','The species has only been recorded indoors during clear weather.'],['Moth 20 / Unassigned','A small specimen with no stable colour record.','The archive disagrees on whether it was seen or merely counted.'],['Copper Margin Moth','Coppery edges and a black centre line.','Its shadow has a different wing shape from the moth itself.'],['Evening Index Moth','Fine violet markings in rows of four.','The last row always contains five marks when counted after sunset.'],['Hollow Wing Moth','A dark oval marking near each wing tip.','The markings are holes only when viewed from the doorway.'],['The Registrar','A pale specimen with a narrow red mark.','It is listed as the person responsible for maintaining this guide.']];
